 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: The system SHALL keep every cached sheet in exactly one of two queues, a first-use queue or a reused queue, and SHALL keep no cached sheet outside them.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a newly rendered sheet is admitted to the cache, the system SHALL insert it into the first-use queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a request is served a sheet that was rendered in response to that request, including a request that presents the job ticket issued for that render, the system SHALL NOT move that sheet into the reused queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When a request that is neither the request that caused a sheet to be rendered nor a request presenting the job ticket issued for that render is served from a sheet held in the first-use queue, the system SHALL move that sheet into the reused queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When a sheet is moved into the reused queue, the system SHALL make that sheet the most recently used sheet in the reused queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When a request is served from a sheet held in the reused queue, the system SHALL make that sheet the most recently used sheet in the reused queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When admitting a sheet to the first-use queue would push that queue past its byte budget, the system SHALL evict the sheets in that queue that were admitted earliest until that queue's total bytes, including the admitted sheet, are within the budget.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When moving a sheet into the reused queue would push that queue past its byte budget, the system SHALL evict the sheets in that queue that were served least recently until that queue's total bytes, including the moved sheet, are within the budget.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: The system SHALL keep the first-use queue's total bytes at or below 2.5 GiB and the reused queue's total bytes at or below 9.5 GiB.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: If a newly rendered sheet's JPEG data is larger than the first-use queue's byte budget, the system SHALL serve it to the requesting client without adding it to the cache.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-016**: When a cache request causes a sheet to be moved between queues or causes a sheet to be evicted, the system SHALL return the same outcome it would have returned without that movement or eviction.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-017**: When concurrent requests are served from the same sheet held in the first-use queue, the system SHALL move that sheet into the reused queue once.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-018**: When a sheet is evicted from the cache, the system SHALL delete its cached JPEG data and SHALL NOT delete any source footage.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-019**: The system SHALL keep temporary render output outside the two cached-sheet queues and SHALL remove that output when the render job completes or fails.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-020**: The system SHALL run at most four render jobs at once and SHALL start render jobs in the order they were enqueued.
